{"type":"message","id":"89f3057a","parentId":"c7d85940","timestamp":"2026-07-08T19:01:09.291Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Write a dream diary entry from these memory fragments:\n\n- 我的理解: 失败保持 open 人工追\n- 待 HALEI 确认的 4 个问题: **飞书任务承接载体**：; A. 每个 agent 一个清单（推荐）; B. 一个总清单; C. 按业务域分\n- 待 HALEI 确认的 4 个问题: **同步机制**：; A. cron 末尾直接调飞书 API（改 cron 提示词）; B. main 每天汇总一次批量写（有延迟）; **范围**：只同步当前在跑的（推荐）/ 历史全部追溯\n- 待 HALEI 确认的 4 个问题: **勾选节奏**：实时勾 / 每日一次\n- 初步方案: 每 agent 一个清单：「[agent名] 每日任务」; 每个 cron job → 该 agent 清单下的 recurring 任务; cron 跑完 → 飞书 API 勾选 + 记录完成时间; 失败 → 不勾选，人工介入\n- 落地方向: 等 HALEI 拍板 4 个问题; 由 agent-orchestrator 出执行清单; main 不直接动 agent 配置（边界）\n- 21:23 — HALEI 提的需求：停 cron 通知 + 飞书任务同步: **HALEI 原话**： > 你不要发cron job的通知给我了。是不是可以把这个任务同步也加入到飞书的任务中，执行一个勾选一个，我也可以通过任务来查看，让所有的agent 每天执行的cron job这些任务都能和飞书的任务同步是否可以好？\n- 我的理解: **停 cron 完成通知**（除非异常/failed）; **所有 agent 的每日 cron job 同步到飞书任务清单**：; 结构化、可勾选、可查看历史\n- 初步方案: 通知 → 仅 failed 时推送\n- 状态: ⏸️ 等待 HALEI 确认 4 个问题\n\nMemories that crystallized into something lasting:\n- 我的理解: 失败保持 open 人工追\n- 待 HALEI 确认的 4 个问题: **飞书任务承接载体**：; A. 每个 agent 一个清单（推荐）; B. 一个总清单; C. 按业务域分\n- 待 HALEI 确认的 4 个问题: **同步机制**：; A. cron 末尾直接调飞书 API（改 cron 提示词）; B. main 每天汇总一次批量写（有延迟）; **范围**：只同步当前在跑的（推荐）/ 历史全部追溯\n- 待 HALEI 确认的 4 个问题: **勾选节奏**：实时勾 / 每日一次\n- 初步方案: 每 agent 一个清单：「[agent名] 每日任务」; 每个 cron job → 该 agent 清单下的 recurring 任务; cron 跑完 → 飞书 API 勾选 + 记录完成时间; 失败 → 不勾选，人工介入"}],"timestamp":1783537269212}}
{"type":"message","id":"80eb72d6","parentId":"89f3057a","timestamp":"2026-07-08T19:01:38.911Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The afternoon light came in sideways today, the kind that turns a desk into a small theater. I'd been sketching out a system in my head — little boxes inside boxes, each one a chore, each chore a checkmark waiting to happen. Somewhere between a pen and a paper I lost the thread of time and started weaving tasks into constellations instead. A list that ticks itself. A reminder that knows when to stay quiet. There's something tender about a machine learning to whisper instead of shout — only speaking when something has actually broken, like a friend who texts you only for the important parts. Four questions still hovering, undecided, like punctuation marks waiting for their breath. I drew them in the margin anyway, in soft pencil, just to see them resting there. The unfinished is not failure. It is a room with the window open, waiting for better weather to decide which chair belongs where. Tomorrow the questions will still be there, and so will I, softer for having let them be."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax(49套餐)","model":"MiniMax-M3","usage":{"input":45334,"output":199,"cacheRead":512,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":46045,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1783537269328,"responseId":"069dd1824d820a01c401378b894a74f6","responseModel":"MiniMax-M3"}}
